      "id": 57808,
      "name": "Ronway",
      "username": "Ronway",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-04T04:32:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ketigid\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/k/9fc29f/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ketigid:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I just noticed there's no flavour text on Lost in the Past. Is this the first time flavour is omitted?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>So it doesn't… Probably because of it's big block of text, it does have a lot of instructions after all. The only other card I would of guessed would skip on it would of been the Self-Destruct Sequence, but it shortened the picture rather than dropping flavour text.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>First edition had no flavour text on their environment cards… Just saying!</p>",
